 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? It can be. Many people do, though it' not for everyone. Yes, bring them indoors before the frost gets them. Late frosts can surprise you. Dress them warmly and move them inside before they get cold. Bring the pots inside too, so they don't crack. The bus stops running when it really snows. You' be safer at home, and you' miss less work. Yes, a tyre with a lower pressure rating for winter use is worth it. It gives more grip and stops you from drifting on smooth, slippery roads.",
